// Title: New BgInfo.EXE Custom WMI Query Registry Configuration
// Sigma ID: cd277474-5c52-4423-a52b-ac2d7969902f
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Nasreddine Bencherchali (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2023-08-16 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: persistence, defense-impairment, T1112
// Description: Detects setting of a new registry value related to BgInfo configuration, which can be abused to
//   execute custom WMI query via "BgInfo.exe"
// False positives:
//   - Legitimate WMI query
// References:
//   - Internal Research
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_bginfo_custom_wmi_query.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, microsoft_xdr schema)

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where RegistryKey endswith "\\Software\\Winternals\\BGInfo\\UserFields*" and RegistryValueData startswith "6"
